Device: emulator-5556, UserApp debug build (com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_2542_nitemcard_strike_price_)
Locale: ar-SA (RTL), Dart VM Service render-tree + evaluate() readings.

=== 1. Threshold measurement (ext.flutter evaluate, package:nears_dls/components/nitemcard/n_item_card.dart) ===
_naturalWidth(price, priceStyle(fontSize:18, PublicSans w700, letterSpacing:-0.2), TextScaler.noScaling):
  "18.10"    -> 68.97 px
  "42.54"    -> 77.08 px
  "51.37"    -> 72.68 px
  "57.72"    -> 72.54 px
  "99.99"    -> 77.23 px
  "100.00"   -> 83.69 px
  "123.45"   -> 84.48 px   (still < rowBudget)
  "999.99"   -> 88.84 px   (> rowBudget -> scaled branch)
  "1,299.00" -> 100.59 px

Real rowBudget measured live on the 150dp "Recommended For You" rail (store_screen.dart,
inStore:true NItemCard) = 85.0px (budget 90.0 - gapWidth 5.0), confirmed identically on
3 separate stores/items below.

=== 2. Real-catalog ceiling (read-only SELECT, multi_food_db) ===
SELECT MAX(current_price) FROM items WHERE recommended=1 AND discount>0 (2949 rows scanned):
  highest = "Cotton Balls" (store 58, City Care Chemist Abu Dhabi) price 57.08, -10% -> 51.37
No recommended+discounted item anywhere in the seed catalog reaches a current-price string
wide enough (>85px, i.e. needs a 3-digit AED integer part) to trip `scaled=true`. The
`_priceRow` scaled/Column branch is therefore UNREACHABLE via any real "Recommended For
You" rail card in this environment's current seed data — confirmed by direct measurement,
not inference.

=== 3. Live render-tree constraint readings (ext.flutter.debugDumpRenderTree), 3 real cards ===
All three are `recommended=1` + discounted items, live on their store's "Recommended For
You" rail (150dp NItemCard, inStore:true), Arabic RTL. All three hit the row's 85px budget
below the scale threshold, so `scaled=false` for every one of them, taking the Row/
`_discountPriceRowFlex` branch (NOT the new Column/stacked branch under test) and
reproducing NEARS-2564's pre-existing near-zero-width-strike signature:

  a) "Double Bacon Burger" (item 419, Spice Route Kitchen, zone 1 / Dhaka)
