=== 4. Structural code guarantee (source read, n_item_card.dart lines 444-472) ===
`if (scaled) { return Column(mainAxisSize: min, children: [Text(originalPrice),
SizedBox, Text(price, stackedCurrentStyle)]) }` — both Text children are DIRECT,
non-Expanded/non-Flexible children of a Column. Flutter's RenderFlex gives every
non-flex child of a vertical Flex the SAME (loosened) width constraint = the
Column's own incoming maxWidth (RenderFlex.performLayout, cross-axis sizing) —
this is deterministic framework behaviour, not something that can regress per-item.
It structurally CANNOT produce the asymmetric near-zero-width split seen in items
(a)-(c) above, because that asymmetry is a property of the Row+Flexible(flex:N)
`_discountPriceRowFlex` branch (the `scaled=false` path), which none of items
(a)-(c) escape (their natural width never exceeds the 85px threshold).

=== Conclusion ===
AC1 (RTL) verdict: PASS by structural + measured proof. The scaled/stacked Column
branch is not reachable with any real "Recommended For You" catalog item in this
seed DB (verified exhaustively, 2949 candidates), so a live pixel-for-pixel
demonstration of the NEW branch was not obtainable through normal driving. In its
place: (1) the exact real-catalog threshold was measured on-device via the app's
own TextPainter-backed `_naturalWidth`, proving no seed item can reach it; (2) 3
live cards -- including the ORIGINAL failing item ("Double Bacon Burger") -- were
re-driven in RTL and geometrically confirmed to reproduce NEARS-2564 (pre-existing,
separately tracked), not a NEARS-2542 defect, matching the conductor's independent
finding; (3) the Column branch's symmetric-width guarantee is a deterministic
Flutter framework property of the actual shipped code (n_item_card.dart:444-472),
not an assumption.
Widgetbook (packages' own storybook, `widgetbook/`) was attempted as a way to force
a genuinely-scaled render with a synthetic long price, but Chrome DevTools MCP had
no reachable page/browser target in this sandbox and the web-driving fallback
(scripts/app-nav/uinav_web.py) requires Playwright, which is not installed in this
environment -- flagged as a followup, not fixed here.
